 Stated plainly, because a plan that hides its constraints is a plan that fails late.
 
+## 0. The scoring mask is narrower than it looks (staff-confirmed)
+
+DrivenData staff [state in the forum](https://community.drivendata.org/t/11516/4)
+that **only the supplied training-label pixels are masked from evaluation in both
+phases**. Predictions 1–3 px from those pixels are **not** exempt from
+false-positive cost unless they are near *new-fault truth*, and the new truth may
+include corrections within 300 m of mapped faults. Consequences, stated once and
+carried everywhere else in this repo:
+
+* Our catalogue blocked-CV DTI is a score on "rediscover the catalogue in held-out
+  blocks" — it is **not** a score on the population the platform evaluates, and
+  nothing here should be read as a score estimate for the hidden faults.
+* Emission adjacent to mapped faults is *not* free: under the staff's masked
+  population, a 1–3 px offset from a training-label pixel is still charged at the
+  full false-positive weight unless it lands on new truth we cannot know about.
+* The Phase-2 write-up (`data/evidence/geology_dossier.md`) carries the same
+  caveat per candidate: proximity to the catalogue is a distance class, not a
+  licence to emit.
+
